      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nBefore: in `SlidingWindowManager.find_longest_cache_hit`, when no full window of cached blocks is found, the cached run at the start of the prompt is used as the hit. With EAGLE and `alignment_tokens > block_size`, that run is aligned twice. It is re-aligned by its length *before* the EAGLE block is dropped, then the EAGLE block is dropped and the result is aligned again. The first alignment is wrong for EAGLE: the run already ends at a block that is aligned *after* the drop, so the hit loses up to one alignment unit.\r\n\r\nExample: block size 2, `alignment_tokens=6`, sliding window 20, EAGLE on, blocks 0-10 cached and block 11 not. The run ends at block 9 (aligned for EAGLE: 9 * 2 % 6 == 0). The hit should be blocks 0-8 = 18 tokens, but the function returns 12 tokens.\r\n\r\nAfter: the first re-alignment is removed. Without EAGLE it was a no-op, because the run always ends at an aligned block. With EAGLE the drop lands on an aligned length. The existing re-alignment after the EAGLE drop is kept.\r\n\r\nThis only changes how much of a cached prefix is reused (a shorter hit was still correct). It does not change model outputs, so no model eval is included.\r\n\r\nNot a duplicate: I searched open PRs and issues for sliding-window / EAGLE / alignment prefix-cache fixes. The closest, #51295, fixes the EAGLE drop in the hybrid coordinator, not this fallback path in `SlidingWindowManager`, which is unchanged on main.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npytest tests/v1/core/test_single_type_kv_cache_manager.py tests/v1/core/prefix_cache \\\r\n  tests/v1/core/test_prefix_caching.py tests/v1/core/test_kv_cache_utils.py \\\r\n  tests/v1/core/test_swa_inflight_window_free.py tests/v1/core/test_prefix_replay.py \\\r\n  tests/v1/core/test_scheduler.py\r\n```\r\n\r\nRun on this branch and on its parent commit on main, on 1x A40. The new test `test_sliding_window_eagle_prefix_hit_keeps_alignment_unit` reproduces the example above.\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n- The new test fails on main (`hit_length == 12`, expected 18) and passes with this change.\r\n- 1x A40, the command above:\r\n  - this branch: 617 passed, 4 failed, 2 errors\r\n  - main (parent commit): 616 passed, 4 failed, 2 errors\r\n  - The only difference is the new test. The 4 failures are pipeline-parallel tests that need more than one GPU (\"World size ... is larger than the number of available GPUs (1)\"), and the 2 errors are `test_hybrid_prefix_cache_hit_rate.py` e2e cases that start `vllm serve`; both are identical on main.\r\n- `pre-commit run` passes on the changed files.\r\n\r\nAI assistance: AI assistance was used during development.\r\n",
